# Build output
bin/
obj/
artifacts/

# The WinDivert driver is fetched, never committed. See tools/fetch-windivert.ps1 and ADR W-0001:
# vendoring a third-party kernel driver is a supply-chain decision that should be made explicitly
# rather than inherited by everyone who clones the repository.
#
# Anchored with a leading slash, and it has to stay that way. Unanchored, "runtime/" matches a
# directory of that name at any depth - and on Windows, where git matches case-insensitively, it
# quietly swallowed src/SplitLane.Engine/Runtime/. Four source files never reached the repository
# and the published branch did not compile, while every local build was green.
/runtime/

# Local solution state
*.user
.vs/
